# SlushAI 3D Modeller - Crontab Configuration Example
#
# To install this crontab:
# 1. Copy this file to a safe location
# 2. Edit the path below to match your installation directory
# 3. Run: crontab -e
# 4. Copy the lines below into your crontab
# 5. Save and exit
#
# To view your current crontab: crontab -l
# To remove all cron jobs: crontab -r

# ============================================================================
# MONTHLY ANALYTICS REPORT
# ============================================================================
# Runs at 2:00 AM on the 1st of every month
# Generates analytics report and cleans up old daily stats
#
# Format: minute hour day month dayofweek command
# 0 2 1 * * = 2:00 AM on the 1st of each month
#
# IMPORTANT: Replace /path/to/AI3DModeller with your actual installation path!
# Example: /Users/YourName/Desktop/Projects/AI3DModeller

0 2 1 * * cd /path/to/AI3DModeller && /usr/bin/python3 scripts/generate_monthly_report.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: DATABASE MAINTENANCE
# ============================================================================
# Vacuum database weekly to reclaim space
# Runs at 3:00 AM every Sunday
#
# Uncomment the line below to enable:
# 0 3 * * 0 cd /path/to/AI3DModeller && /usr/bin/sqlite3 logs/analytics.db "VACUUM;" >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: BACKUP DATABASES
# ============================================================================
# Backup user and analytics databases daily at 4:00 AM
# Keeps last 7 days of backups
#
# Uncomment the lines below to enable:
# 0 4 * * * cd /path/to/AI3DModeller && cp logs/users.db logs/backups/users_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d).db && find logs/backups/ -name "users_*.db" -mtime +7 -delete >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
# 0 4 * * * cd /path/to/AI3DModeller && cp logs/analytics.db logs/backups/analytics_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d).db && find logs/backups/ -name "analytics_*.db" -mtime +7 -delete >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ============================================================================
# CRON TIME SYNTAX REFERENCE
# ============================================================================
# * * * * * command to execute
# ┬ ┬ ┬ ┬ ┬
# │ │ │ │ │
# │ │ │ │ └─── Day of week (0-7, Sunday=0 or 7)
# │ │ │ └───── Month (1-12)
# │ │ └─────── Day of month (1-31)
# │ └───────── Hour (0-23)
# └─────────── Minute (0-59)
#
# Examples:
# 0 0 * * * = Daily at midnight
# 0 2 1 * * = Monthly at 2 AM on the 1st
# 0 */4 * * * = Every 4 hours
# 30 9 * * 1-5 = Weekdays at 9:30 AM
# 0 0 * * 0 = Weekly on Sunday at midnight

# ============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================================================
# If cron isn't working:
#
# 1. Check cron is running:
#    - Linux: sudo systemctl status cron
#    - macOS: sudo launchctl list | grep cron
#
# 2. Check cron logs:
#    - Linux: grep CRON /var/log/syslog
#    - macOS: grep cron /var/log/system.log
#
# 3. Verify Python path:
#    which python3
#    (Use this path instead of /usr/bin/python3 if different)
#
# 4. Test command manually:
#    cd /path/to/AI3DModeller && python3 scripts/generate_monthly_report.py
#
# 5. Check permissions:
#    chmod +x scripts/generate_monthly_report.py
#    mkdir -p logs/backups
#
# 6. macOS only: Grant cron Full Disk Access
#    System Preferences > Security & Privacy > Full Disk Access
#    Add /usr/sbin/cron or Terminal app
